// Power : Grave Robber XP Debt Greater 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Day Job Jet Pack 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Display Name :
"P3275746375" "Traveler's Jet Pack"
// Power Help Text :
"P1988900856" "Your hard work from your Day Job has given you access to a Jet Pack.  The Traveler's Jetpack will allow you to fly for as long as there is enough fuel.  Logging out in Grandville or The Shadow Shard will earn you additional usage time for your Traveler's Jet Pack."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Architect Ticket Lesser 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Display Name :
"P3099060277" "Architect"
// Power Mouse-Over Text :
"P2589529727" "Auto: Ticket Bonus"
// Power Help Text :
"P3462774782" "Your day job will grant you a 5%% ticket bonus upon completion of a Mission Architect mission as long as time remains on this power."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Architect Ticket Greater 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Display Name :
"P2169225473" "Experienced Architect"
// Power Help Text :
"P3683613305" "Your day job will grant you a 10%% ticket bonus upon completion of a Mission Architect mission as long as time remains on this power."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Warden Baton 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Display Name :
"P2082248681" "Baton"
// Power Mouse-Over Text :
"P2760137029" "Melee Minor DMG (Smashing) Foe Disorient"
// Power Help Text :
"P3274935322" "Your authority gained from working in both law enforcement and for the city government has earned you usage of a Baton.  Foes struck in melee combat with this weapon will suffer minor damage, but each strike has a high chance of disorienting the target.  Additional uses of this power can be earned by logging out in either City Hall or a Police Station.  Damage: Minor, Recharge: Very Fast"
// DisplayTargetShortHelp :
// DisplayTargetHelp :
"P2418887360" "You have been disoriented"
// Effect AttackerHit Message :
"P2948532509" "You smash {PlayerDest} with your {PowerName} for {Damage} points of smashing damage."
// Effect VictimHit Message :
// Effect AttackerHit Message :
"P3123854675" "You disorient {PlayerDest} with your {PowerName}."
// Effect VictimHit Message :
"P777389710" "{PlayerSource} disorients you with their {PowerName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Security Guard Tear Gas 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power Help Text :
"P1288730718" "Your time as a security guard and police officer has earned you access to Tear Gas.  Foes affected by the gas will be left choking and held for a short duration.  Additional Tear Gas canisters can be earned by logging out in a Police Station or Vault.  Recharge: Long."
// Effect AttackerHit Message :
"P2700203249" "You hold {PlayerDest} with your {PowerName}"
// Effect VictimHit Message :
"P2985970520" "{PlayerSource} holds you with their {PowerName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Scientist Sleep Grenade 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Display Name :
"P855281558" "Sleep Gas"
// Power Mouse-Over Text :
// Power Help Text :
"P1985434512" "Your time studying various sciences has earned you access to Sleep Grenades.  Foes affected by the gas will be put to sleep for a short while.  Sleeping foes will awaken if they suffer damage.  Additional Sleep Gas canisters can be earned by logging out in a University, inside Portal Corps (Heroes) or inside the Crey Industries building (Villains).  Recharge: Long."
// DisplayTargetShortHelp :
"P4293364200" "Sleeping"
// DisplayTargetHelp :
"P1932299114" "You have been put to sleep by the Sleep Gas."
// Effect AttackerHit Message :
"P1270298" "Your {PowerName} puts {PlayerDest} to sleep."
// Effect VictimHit Message :
"P2161698613" "{PlayerSource} puts you to sleep with their {PowerName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Doctor Revive Ally 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Display Name :
"P2754785057" "Revive Ally"
// Power Help Text :
"P348265684" "Your time spent studying medicine has gained you access to a medical kit that allows you to revive a nearby fallen ally.  Allies revived by this power will be healed for a small portion of their health and be protected from XP Debt for 15 seconds.  Additional charges of this power can be earned by logging out in a hospital or university.  Recharge: Very Long."
// DisplayConfirm :
"P972847107" "{PlayerSource} would like to Revive you.  You will be revived with XP Debt protection, a moderate amount of health, but no endurance. Do you Accept?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Alchemists Potion 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Display Name :
"P39485835" "Vitalize"
// Power Mouse-Over Text :
// Power Help Text :
"P3967715340" "Your knowledge of both medicine and magic has taught you how to heal your allies.  Use this power on an ally to recover a portion of their health.  Additional charges of Vitalize can be gained by logging out in a Hospital or the Midnighter's Club.  Recharge: Long."
// Effect AttackerHit Message :
// Effect VictimHit Message :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Soldier Grenade 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Display Name :
"P673762878" "Fragmentation Grenade"
// Power Mouse-Over Text :
"P2726244704" "Targeted AoE Moderate DMG (Lethal/Smashing), Foe Knockback"
// Power Help Text :
"P3567314222" "Your military training with Vanguard and from being on Patrol has earned you access to Fragmentation Grenades.  When thrown, these grenades will deal moderate lethal and smashing damage to all enemies within the area of effect and have a chance to knock them back.  Additional grenades can be earned by logging out in a Vanguard Base or while on Patrol.  Damage: Moderate, Recharge: Slow."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Rapid Response Member Teleport 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Display Name :
"P1239539082" "Base Teleporter"
// Power Mouse-Over Text :
// Power Help Text :
"P1321718707" "You have earned the ability to teleport back to your supergroup base from your diligent duty on patrol and guarding your base.  Using this power will teleport you back to your supergroup and it can be used once every 15 minutes.  Additional uses of this power can be gained by logging out on Patrol or back at your Supergroup base.  Recharge: Very Long."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Trend Setter Placate 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Display Name :
"P3534004199" "Beguile"
// Power Help Text :
"P3754350714" "Your time spent hob-nobbing at Pocket D has earned you the ability to convince enemies to temporarily not attack you.  You can placate a single foe at range and call off their attack briefly.  You can earn additional uses of this power by logging out at Pocket D or a Tailor.  Recharge: Very Long."
// Effect VictimHit Message :
"P1864267621" "You have been Placated and cannot target {PlayerSource}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Time Traveler 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Display Name :
"P4270535135" "Time Lord's Boon"
// Power Mouse-Over Text :
"P2768896904" "Auto: Self +Recharge, Res (Slow, Teleport)"
// Power Help Text :
"P419871296" "Traveling back and forth through time is not without its benefits.  You have a slightly increased attack rate and are resistant to both slows, and will usually protect yourself from being teleported by enemies, this power is always on.  You can gain additional time for this effect by logging out in either Cimerora. or Ouroboros."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Archaelogist Rune 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Display Name :
"P2449104955" "Rune of Purification"
// Power Mouse-Over Text :
"P3547151724" "Ranged, Moderate DMG(Energy)/Special vs. Non Human"
// Power Help Text :
"P4111525419" "Your time spent studying ancient relics and magical artifacts has earned you access to the Rune of Purification.  This rune will deal moderate energy damage to a target, non-human targets will suffer additional damage.  You can gain additional charges of this power by logging off in a Graveyard or the Midnighter's Club.  Damage: Moderate, Recharge: Long."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Combat Shield 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Display Name :
"P535102080" "Combat Shield"
// Power Help Text :
"P3804813294" "Your rigorous training in the arena and on the battlefield has given you access to the Combat Shield.  While this power is active you have increased defense to Lethal, Smashing and Energy attacks.  Additional time can be gained on this power by logging out in either a PvP zone or in an arena.  Recharge: Fast."
// Power AttackerHit Message :
"P959440686" "You Combat Shield increased you Defense to Lethal, Smashing, and to some degree, Energy attacks."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Web Weaver Grenade 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power Help Text :
"P3656670509" "Your work with Arachnos has earned you access to web grenades.  When these grenades come in contact with their target they will immobilize them as well reducing their movement and attack speed as well as preventing them from flying.  Additional grenades can be earned by logging out in an Arachnos Base or the Arachnos Building in Port Oakes.  Recharge: Fast."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Black Ops Smoke Grenade 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power Help Text :
"P1043887910" "Your training from working with Arachnos and several successful heists has earned you access to Smoke Bombs.  The Smoke Bomb envelops all those in the affected area in a cloud of smoke. Most foes will not be able to see past normal melee range, although some may have better perception. If the villains are attacked, they will be alerted to your presence, but will suffer a penalty to their chance to hit.  Additional bombs can be earned by logging out at an Arachnos Base or at a Vault.  Recharge: Long."
// DisplayTargetHelp :
"P4189912123" "Your visual range and Chance to hit has been reduced by the Smoke Bomb."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Entrepreneur Crafting Discount 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Display Name :
"P2900090933" "Entrepreneur Crafting Discount"
// Power Mouse-Over Text :
"P1779946623" "Auto: Crafting Cost Discount"
// Power Help Text :
"P4093891018" "Your experience working with the auction house or black market coupled with your knowledge of running a business has taught you how to get the most out of what you have on hand.  You will gain a number of discount tokens that will reduce crafting costs by 25%.  These tokens can be obtained by logging out at in a shop (Hero) or docks (Villains) or near Wentworth's (Hero) or the Black Market (Villains)."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Master Architect Power 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Display Name :
// Power Help Text :
"P736239274" "Your experience studying virtual environments and knowing the ins and outs of the Architect has earned you the You're able to shrug off the effects of simulated defeat once every 10 minutes while on Architect missions.  This will revive you with a small amount of hit points and no endurance, but you'll have 90 seconds of XP Debt Protection."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Power : Analysts Teleporter 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Display Name :
"P1873515504" "Analyst's Teleporter"
// Power Help Text :
"P3384112475" "Your knowledge of portal technologies has earned you access to the Analyst's Teleporter power.  Using this power you'll be able to teleport great distances instantaneously by clicking this power and selecting a distant location.  You will earn charges for this power by logging out in the Rift Enclosure."

